; Divide in AUTO: 25 / 5
; E.S.R.'s way: the dividend complemented, the divisor in M, the MQ at 7,
; OVERFLOW set to HALT, AUTO, START. The machine adds M cycle after cycle
; and stops itself at the overflow: the MQ read the other way (7 - MQ) is
; the cycles begun. A at 0 there means it went exactly: that is the
; quotient. (Otherwise the hand would finish the cycle, UNTIL CYCLE in
; MANUAL, and read it as programs/divide.dc2 does: the quotient one less,
; the remainder M - A. A halt can stop mid-cycle at A = 0 when it isn't
; exact, 11 / 5 for one, so that is always the safe way.)

R               ; reset
SET A 25        ; the dividend
X Space X Space ; complement it: A = 103 = 128 - 25
SET M 5         ; the divisor
SET MQ 7        ; the counter
D               ; distributor set to begin a cycle
M               ; MULTIPLY on
OVERFLOW HALT
AUTO
RUN             ; five cycles, the last stopped by the overflow
MANUAL
OVERFLOW RUN
CHECK A 0       ; it went exactly
CHECK MQ 2      ; 7 - 2 = 5 cycles: 25 / 5 = 5
